steps.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve. Input 1 is the identity and exact composition reference; use ONLY its BOTTOM-RIGHT cell (JASPE standing upright behind her desk) as the master for all FOUR cells of a new speaking sprite sheet.
Output exact 1536x1024 PNG, 2x2 equally sized 768x512 cells, no gutters/borders/text. Repeat the same bottom-right standing pose, same head and body scale, camera, desk registration, pale blue #eaf4fc backdrop and lighting in every cell. Same recognizable girl: two curly puff buns with central braids, big brown eyes, warm brown skin, tiny earrings, navy pinafore, white short-sleeve shirt, striped tie. Her entire head, hair and hands remain within each cell. ONLY upper body visible; waist/lower body naturally occluded by the desk. No legs or feet.
Animate a gentle TWO-HANDED explanation while STANDING, not seated: 
1 top-left: standing straight, hands just lifted a little above the desk near the middle, lips nearly closed in soft smile;
2 top-right: both forearms lift to lower chest, palms open upwards, mouth softly open speaking;
3 bottom-left: both hands spread slightly apart naturally, one a little higher, palms upward, lips rounded saying oh;
4 bottom-right: hands lower toward the desk again, friendly smile, preparing to loop.
Keep gestures restrained and anatomically coherent, fingers relaxed, shoulders/head nearly still, exact same head size in all frames. In particular, never return her to the seated/cheek-supported pose. Desk, closed navy book on the left and pencil cup on the right remain fixed in every cell. This is a 2D raster sprite asset, no new 3D model. No identity drift, no other characters, no extra limbs, no text or UI.
